Package: openmux-factory-tools
Version: 1.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OpenMux <support@openmux.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenMux
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: usbutils, python3-serial
Description: OpenMux factory provisioning and test tools
 Standalone factory utilities for the OpenMux console: programming the
 internal/external FTDI EEPROM (manufacturer, product, serial base),
 a topology scan that tells the console's own FTDI chips apart from a
 plug-in EX-12 adapter by where each chip hangs on USB (they share one
 VID:PID, and an unprogrammed chip has no serial to tell them apart
 by), an audit that checks every /dev/openmux/portN against the
 USB interface the udev rules promise it, a serial loopback test and
 the board test runner. The flashers refuse the console's chips when
 handed a card and refuse a card when handed the console, and re-read
 each chip immediately before writing it because flashing re-numbers
 the hub. Installed on the install medium (used from the factory
 menu) and on the target (kept for field service). Flashing needs the
 ftdi_eeprom binary, which this image does not ship; the tools report
 that and stop rather than half-running.
